                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Due to how Steam handles reviews and their moderation, I didn't want to write any more reviews, but I think I should write one for this game so people don't waste money on it.\n\nNot bad idea for a small game, but it suffers from so much unfinish-unpolish syndrome that I can't recommend this unless you get it for free. It feels more like an afternoon project waiting to be finished. I made a post about these issues and no word from the developer about this or other users' posts, so I must guess the dev just abandoned the project. I'll happily change this review if game is ever updated.\n\nThere's no controller support. Keyboard does well, but this game begs for controllers.\nThe game is played with keyboard, but the initial menu uses mouse. Neither coherent nor convenient.\nSettings don't stay. I have to change to full screen manually each time I launch the game.\nAchievements don't work. Plus their icons don't show either. This has been known and reported since launch day, and not fixed.\nThere are no sound effects at all. It should be basic to have at least jump, death and entering gate.\nThe music stops after a while. It doesn't even loop. So after about 2 minutes of gameplay, the game is fully silent. This only happens while playing - on the menu the music apparently loops. It's also inconsistent, sometimes it does loop.\nThere should be a pointer about the double jump, as I discovered it by pure accident.\nNot sure of the number of levels - if there are only the levels presented in the main menu, game is too short.\n\nOverall controls feel too ice-skating, and the double jump is not very well done IMHO; that's a matter of opinions, not very good for me but not game breaking either.\n\nI think the game had potential to be fun, as it's a simple idea that really works as intended, but well, too many troubles to care about it anymore. Avoid.",
